# Java & Quarkus Standards

Enforcement: **B**. Prefer project conventions over this file when they conflict with evidence in-repo.

## Design

- Apply SOLID/DRY/KISS with restraint — see `software-architecture.mdc`.
- Package by feature or bounded context when the codebase already does; do not reorganize casually.
- Introduce interfaces/factories only for multiple implementations, testing seams that pay for themselves, or framework requirements.
- Prefer immutable data where practical; minimize shared mutable state.

## Quarkus / CDI

- Use CDI beans with appropriate scope (`@ApplicationScoped`, `@RequestScoped`, etc.).
- Constructor injection preferred; avoid field injection in new code unless matching local style.
- Config via MicroProfile Config / `%profile` properties — no hardcoded env-specific values in code.
- Distinguish blocking vs non-blocking (reactive) paths; do not block event-loop threads.
- Use Quarkus extensions already in the project before adding new ones.

## REST & APIs

- Clear resource naming; consistent error bodies; correct status codes.
- Validate input (Bean Validation) at the boundary.
- Backward-compatible API evolution; deprecate before remove.
- Authn/z at the edge; never rely on “hidden” URLs.

## Data & transactions

- Explicit transaction boundaries (`@Transactional` wisely — not on every method).
- Connection pools sized from evidence; never leak connections/streams.
- Use parameterized queries / repository APIs; no string-built SQL.
- For multi-service consistency, see `microservices.mdc` (outbox/saga) — do not invent XA lightly.

## Concurrency & performance

- Thread safety for shared mutable state; prefer concurrent utilities over home-rolled locks.
- Avoid premature optimization; measure before caching.
- Mind JVM memory: allocations in hot paths, N+1 queries, unbounded collections.

## Observability

- Structured logging with correlation IDs; no secrets in logs.
- Metrics and traces via existing Quarkus OpenTelemetry / Micrometer setup when present.

## Testing (when applicable)

| Layer | Typical tools |
|-------|----------------|
| Unit | JUnit 5, Mockito |
| Integration | `@QuarkusTest`, Testcontainers |
| API | RestAssured / HTTP tests |
| Contract | Pact or project equivalent |
| Architecture | ArchUnit if already used |
| Performance | Only with clear SLO and harness |

Match the repo’s existing test stack. Record commands and exit codes — never fabricate.

## Dependencies

- Prefer BOM / Quarkus platform alignment.
- Justify new dependencies; check licenses and CVE posture with available tools.
